From d3aedc3173589a04e8dd8d4514925a4089a3c19e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 21:21:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add A4 book target to the typesetting pipeline

Adds `--ziel druck-a4`: the same book, the same Satzmuster page design
(mirrored margins, marginal column, running heads, blank verso before
each chapter), laid out on A4 instead of 170 x 240 mm.

The type size does not scale with the page. 10 pt on a 13 pt baseline
stays; the main column grows only from 95 to 115 mm (~64 characters) and
the extra width goes to the marginal column and the margins. The A4 text
block is an exact 51 x 13 pt, so unlike the 170 x 240 block it ends on a
baseline instead of between two.

`druckpruefung.py` no longer hardcodes 170 x 240. It recognises which of
the built formats a file is in and then checks every page against it,
which also catches a single odd-sized sheet inside the block -- the old
version only ever looked at page one.

Measured, not assumed: druck 283 pages and bildschirm 190 pages are
unchanged, druck-a4 is 211 pages, fonts embedded on all three, and the
A4 build carries at least as much text as the approved print build (it
has fewer mid-word line breaks, not more).

The Buchkonzept 1.2 still names 17 x 24 cm as the target format; this
adds an edition beside it, it does not replace it.

